<title>BELGIUM: US is top 96 cargo destination for AEA carriers.</title>
<headline>US is top 96 cargo destination for AEA carriers.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. was the top cargo destination for European carriers in 1996, Association of European Airlines (AEA) figures showed.</p>
<p>The top 10 destinations in tonnes, were as follows:</p>
<p>    1.  U.S.	 1,152,000</p>
<p>    2.  Japan	  190,000</p>
<p>    3.  India	  152,000</p>
<p>    4.  Hong Kong    116,000</p>
<p>    5.  Canada	 105,000</p>
<p>    6.  Singapore     92,000</p>
<p>    7.  South Africa  82,000</p>
<p>    8.  Brazil	  70,000</p>
<p>    9.  Korea	   57,000</p>
<p>    10. Kenya	   56,000</p>
<p>AEA said it was issuing these figures for the first time. They do not represent overall air cargo ex-Europe to the destinations as cargo flown by non-European carriers is not included. - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
